Review the documentation diff on branch `design/opencode-plugin-adapter` in <repo>, read-only: `git diff 01ee06b..HEAD -- docs/design-opencode-plugin.md DESIGN.md CHANGELOG.md .github/workflows/biff-notify.yml`.

These are rounds 4–5 of a design document (DES-078) for an OpenCode plugin, a CHANGELOG entry, and a CI workflow change.

Check for:
- factual claims about the code that are false (verify cited file:line against source);
- internal contradictions between `docs/design-opencode-plugin.md` and DES-078 in DESIGN.md;
- CLAUDE.md-rule violations;
- in the workflow: secret exposure, unpinned actions, or a trigger that hands secrets to fork code.

Do not edit anything. Report only high-confidence findings, each with file:line and a concrete fix. Report zero findings if there are none.

Review, read-only, the design diff on branch `design/opencode-plugin-adapter` in <repo>: `git diff 01ee06b..HEAD -- docs/design-opencode-plugin.md DESIGN.md`.

The design makes claims that are your target. Verify each against the code it cites (internal/session/store.go, internal/mission/active.go, internal/hook/pretooluse_dispatch.go, internal/hook/commit_trailers.go, plugin/hooks/commit-msg.sh, internal/enable/enable.go) and against docs/spec-opencode-integration.tex:
- fail-closed on every ambiguous attribution path;
- lineage written once and never changed;
- purge never reclaims a live OpenCode session (isStale uses max(Started, LastSeen));
- claim-forked never leaves an orphan skeleton;
- three distinct exit statuses;
- lock order: NewID, mission lock, delegation lock, child dispatch-pending lock outermost;
- neither harness privileged in enable/disable;
- the supported-harness list is a single source of truth.

For each claim, report one of: holds, holds with a stated gap, or false. Give file:line and a concrete fix for each false one. Do not edit anything.
